LIMIT sdk-versions protocol versions the installed MCP SDK can negotiate
PASS  filesystem-connect connection, identity and negotiated version
LIMIT recorded-protocol-version the negotiated protocol version is recorded for a stdio server
PASS  filesystem-tools-list tools/list: RigorRun sees every tool the server offers
FAIL  filesystem-call tools/call and normalisation of a prose result
PASS  filesystem-error a refused call is an error, never data
PASS  filesystem-teardown close() ends the stdio child
PASS  memory-structured a structured result is read as records
PASS  memory-teardown close() ends the stdio child
LIMIT tools-list-pagination tools/list follows nextCursor
PASS  normalisation-structured structuredContent is records
PASS  normalisation-json-in-text JSON inside a text block is records (R-8)
PASS  normalisation-prose prose is never records
PASS  errors isError results and JSON-RPC errors are errors, not data
LIMIT normalisation-links-and-images resource_link and image-only results
PASS  timeout a call past its timeout is an error, not an empty result
LIMIT stderr-flood a server writing 200 KB to stderr is still answered
exit 0
